-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
version  1.0.0.0  |  2024-09-11  |
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIX Remove unused TAPI ring set cadence. Add missing mutex release in case of
    pTxData null pointer.
CHG Move classic TAPI compatibility symbol to separate header file to avoid
    include of drv_tapi_config.h when external applications/libraries use
    drv_tapi_io.h file. [VOICECPE_SW-2630]
CHG Deactivate tone generator level compensation by default. [VOICECPE_SW-2654]
CHG Improve README file content. [VOICECPE_SW-2630]
CHG Add register number to TAPI debug buffer logs. [VOICECPE_SW-2647]
CHG Add initialization checkpoints to TAPI debug buffer log. [VOICECPE_SW-2647]
FIX Event logger integration. [VOICECPE_SW-2630]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
version  0.9.1.0  |  2024-06-27  |
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIX IOCTL indexes/handlers mismatch when CLASSIC_TAPI_COMPATIBLE switch is not
    defined. [VOICECPE_SW-2671]
NEW Add support for BBD V2 to handle CIB DC/DC type. [VOICECPE_SW-2663]
FIX Capacity measurements feature must be enabled in order to use phone
    detection functionality. Set DXS capacity measurements feature implicitly
    in case PPD is enabled. [VOICECPE_SW-2664]
NEW Add specific error number for automatic calibration timeout.
    [VOICECPE_SW-2630]
CHG Remove DXS_statusIfxError error code usage which leads to misleading error
    string resolution and use DXS_statusErr instead. [VOICECPE_SW-2630]
FIX Use after free bug when RETURN_STATUS/RETURN_DEVSTATUS tries to report an
    error after TAPI device un-registration is done. [VOICECPE_SW-2665]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
version  0.9.0.0  |  2024-04-17  |
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHG The level of tones played into local direction is automatically corrected
    with the attenuation which is configured in the BBD file for the local
    direction. As result the level of tones on the analog line is defined
    only by the tone configuration and independent from the attenuation
    configured in the BBD file. This includes the level of the FSK signal in
    CID sequences. The range of this compensation is limited to the maximum
    level of the tone generators. This feature is disabled by default but can
    be enabled by providing "--enable-tone-generator-level-compensation"
    during configure stage. [VOICECPE_SW-2654]
FIX Fixed crash in error handling when BBD download is called on device fds
    but data structs are not initialised. [VOICECPE_SW-2660]
CHG Improve TAPI API configure selection. From now --enable-tapi4 can be given
    without the need to set --disable-tapi3. [VOICECPE_SW-2648]
NEW Add support for linux based ARM 32 and 64-bit platforms compilation.
    Compilation is possible by giving correct configure triplets, setting ARCH
    symbol and adding path to toolchain to PATH variable if needed.
    [VOICECPE_SW-2655]
NEW Add procfs entry "debug_level" to set the verbosity level of debug output
    to the console during runtime. [VOICECPE_SW-2652]
NEW Implement TAPI debug buffer which can act as a helper for SPI traffic
    tracing, storing custom user entries. It can be accessed via procfs and
    ioctl interfaces. [VOICECPE_SW-2647]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                  |  2023-11-29  | Test candidate
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEW Create a new Standalone TAPI for the DXS driver by combining TAPI driver
    version 4.26.0.0 and Duslic XS driver version 1.10.0.0 [VOICECPE_SW-2630]
